{
  "id": "30762_suku",
  "headword": "{好|す}く",
  "reading": "すく",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to like; to be fond of",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to like; to be fond of; to take to",
      "explanation": "To feel affection or liking for someone or something. In modern Japanese the plain affirmative is rare; the verb survives mainly in the passive {好|す}かれる (to be liked) and the negative {好|す}かない (to not care for)."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "30762_suku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{皆|みんな}に{好|す}かれている。",
      "english": "She is liked by everyone.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30762_suku_ex2",
      "japanese": "あの{人|ひと}のやり{方|かた}は{好|す}かない。",
      "english": "I don't care for the way that person does things.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30762_suku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{正直|しょうじき}で{気|き}さくな{彼女|かのじょ}は、{職場|しょくば}の{誰|だれ}からも{好|す}かれている。",
      "english": "Honest and easygoing, she is liked by everyone at work.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "USAGE:\nSaying {私|わたし}はあの{人|ひと}を{好|す}く sounds stiff and old-fashioned. Use the na-adjective {好|す}き instead: あの{人|ひと}が{好|す}きだ.\n\nCOMMON FORMS:\n- {好|す}かれる: to be liked (by far the most common form)\n- {好|す}かない: to not care for, to dislike\n- {好|す}き{好|この}んで: out of preference, willingly\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive, taking を: {人|ひと}を{好|す}く. The passive marks the liker with に or から: {皆|みんな}に{好|す}かれる.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {好|この}む: to prefer — a considered choice rather than an emotional pull\n- {気|き}に{入|い}る: to take a liking to — about a particular thing that pleased you",
